            <ArticleTitle>Splenoportovenography in portal hypertension: a safe outpatient procedure.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>146-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Splenoportovenography (SPV) was performed as an outpatient procedure in 172 patients to investigate portal hypertension. Careful technique and proper patient selection were responsible for the high success rate (95.3%) and the low complication rate (7.0%). We conclude that SPV done as an outpatient procedure is safe in expert hands and is economical.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
